---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Tinycord" description="About the Tinycord project" mainClass="py-16 sm:py-20">
  <section class="-mx-4 mb-12 sm:-mx-0">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight m-0">
        About
      </h1>
      <p class="text-secondary mt-3 max-w-lg text-base sm:text-lg">
        The idea behind Tinycord, plain and simple.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <p>
      I made Tinycord because Discord's desktop app shouldn't need a Chromium
      browser just to send messages. The official client is Electron, roughly
      200 MB of disk space and hundreds of MB of RAM, all for a chat app.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tinycord uses your system's native WebView instead. WKWebView on macOS,
      WebView2 on Windows, WebKitGTK on Linux. The result is a binary under
      5 MB with a fraction of the memory usage. Just a native window loading
      Discord's web app, nothing more.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's written in Zig, roughly 50 lines for the app logic. Open a WebView,
      load a URL, handle window events. No heavy runtime, no garbage collector,
      no framework overhead. The OS does the work.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's the whole philosophy. Not adding features, not reinventing Discord.
      Just stripping away what's unnecessary.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-16 grid max-w-2xl gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="border border-default bg-muted p-4">
      <h2 class="m-0 text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-primary">Lightweight</h2>
      <p class="m-0 mt-1 text-sm text-secondary">A binary under 5 MB and minimal RAM. No Electron overhead.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="border border-default bg-muted p-4">
      <h2 class="m-0 text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-primary">Focused</h2>
      <p class="m-0 mt-1 text-sm text-secondary">Does one thing — loads Discord. No features, no clutter.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="border border-default bg-muted p-4">
      <h2 class="m-0 text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-primary">Native</h2>
      <p class="m-0 mt-1 text-sm text-secondary">Built with the OS, not against it. WebView, not Chromium.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="border border-default bg-muted p-4">
      <h2 class="m-0 text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-primary">Open Source</h2>
      <p class="m-0 mt-1 text-sm text-secondary">MIT licensed. Full source on GitHub. Built in public.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
